    "Use only this seven-stage sequence, in order: (1) map liquidity: previous week high/low, previous day high/low, Asian/London/New York session highs/lows when visible, equal highs/lows and confirmed swing highs/lows; (2) identify a liquidity sweep only when price wicks beyond a mapped level and closes back through it; (3) confirm MSS only after the sweep, using a candle close through the relevant opposing swing; (4) confirm directional displacement with clear candle expansion; (5) identify a genuine three-candle fair value gap; (6) wait for price to retrace into that exact FVG; (7) require a separate entry-confirmation candle.",
    "For every stage report CONFIRMED, WAIT, or NOT VISIBLE; give the exact screenshot timeframe, readable price, candle evidence, and timestamp only when visible. Reconstruct earlier stages from the uploaded historical candles/screenshots; do not assume a sweep must happen after the screenshot was taken. Keep EUR/USD and GBP/USD independent.",
